{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>Ox or sheep.</b> Excluding hybrids. Or goat — excluding a non-koshy animal." "<b>When it is born.</b> And not a man. The meaning is: it is not called an ox or sheep or goat, fit for a sacrifice, until it is born. But a man born by caesarean section is fit to bring a sacrifice as one born normally." "<b>And it shall be seven days.</b> Excluding one lacking time, for we are concerned lest it be a miscarriage. Another interpretation: all who separate from a place of foulness and impurity require a seven-day separation before entering the camp of the Divine Presence, such as a zav, and a metzora, and one impure through a corpse. <b>Under its mother.</b> Excluding an orphan. This commandment was already stated in the portion of Mishpatim regarding a firstborn, and here regarding a regular animal." "<b>And from the eighth day and onward.</b> Above, in the portion of Mishpatim, where it says ״and on the eighth day you shall give it to Me״ — that is to dedicate it, and here, to sacrifice it." "<b>It shall be accepted for a fire-offering.</b> After he warned them that it shall not be accepted, he likewise mentioned to them that it shall not be accepted before the eighth day."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:29.871373951Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}